  "audio": "011.keeping-one-dedicated.mp3",
  "paragraph": 11,
  "text": "Keeping one dedicated client per server is not an accident—it gives you clean isolation. Your Slack server never sees what your local files server is reading, and every connection carries only the permissions meant for that specific tool. Better yet, if one server crashes or goes offline mid-session, the rest of your connected workspace keeps running without missing a beat.",
